  <main>
    <h1>ABOUT</h1>
    <p>I'm Nikita.</p>

    <p>I design products. I've been doing it for five years.</p>
    <p>
      I studied business, not design. I started designing because of
      a project of my own: I felt nobody else would get how I wanted it
      to look. Then came work for friends, then a website for a local
      repair and tailoring shop. It's still live.
    </p>
    <p>
      Then Medal, a desktop app for gamers. I worked on avatars and
      rewards, then on how you record the thing that just happened.
      Then crypto: a wallet, an explorer, a set of tools. The wallet
      launched at ETHDenver 2023. The explorer never shipped. None of it
      runs now, for reasons that had nothing to do with design.
    </p>
    <p>
      I've worked in teams and in a studio. Now I design on my own.
      The work I'm proudest of came when the decisions were mine to make.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <p>
      I like to travel, change my surroundings and get deep into a culture
      I don't know yet.
    </p>
    <p>
      I reply to designers on X more than I post. I build my own tools
      with Claude Code. I'm trying to make design experiments a habit,
      and to post each one.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <p>
      That's about it.<br />
      If you want to work together —
    </p>
    <a href="/#review">Send a link, get a video review →</a>
  </main>
